course: dictionary
lesson: 9244
title: Soreness: the ache in your body
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Soreness is a noun. It means pain, an ache, or tenderness in a part of your body. «Soreness a day or two after a race» tells you when it often happens: after hard exercise, not during it.
explain: Other words show the same idea. «Muscle soreness» is an ache in your muscles, «a sore throat» hurts in your throat, and «a sore knee» hurts in your knee. Normal soreness is usually a dull ache that eases in a few days. Sharp pain is different.
explain: There is also a rare, old-fashioned meaning. Someone can still feel «sore» about losing a game, which means upset or annoyed. Check the sentence: if it is about a body part, soreness means pain; if it is about feelings, it means upset.
fact: Soreness means pain, aching or tenderness in a part of the body.
fact: «Normal soreness is a dull ache that eases in a few days.»
fact: «Sharp pain in one spot, swelling, or not being able to put weight on a leg» is not normal, so tell an adult.
fact: Muscle soreness a day or two after unusual exercise is normal, and gentle movement helps.
fact: Rare meaning: soreness can mean being upset or annoyed about something, as in still feeling «sore» about losing.
exercise: «Soreness a day or two after a race comes from tiny muscle strains being repaired.» What does soreness mean here? | *Pain or an ache in the muscles | A kind of sports drink | Being very fast in a race | A cold in the nose
exercise: Which of these is a sign of an injury, not normal soreness? | A mild ache after a race that goes in a few days | A dull ache that eases in a few days | Stiff legs after a long walk | *Sharp pain in one spot, with swelling
exercise: Ravi still feels «sore» about losing the match. What does sore mean here? | Fast and full of energy | Hurt in his leg | Hungry after the match | *Upset or annoyed about losing
test: «Stretching after sport helps keep you flexible, but studies show it does very little to stop next-day soreness.» What does this suggest stretching does for next-day soreness? | Makes it much worse | Causes sharp pain | *Does very little to stop it | Stops it completely
test: In «a sore throat», what does sore mean? | Tired of running | Full of food | *Painful or aching | Very tall
exam: «Lactic acid is cleared within about an hour after exercise, so it does not cause next-day soreness.» What does the sentence tell you about lactic acid and next-day soreness? | Lactic acid makes you hungry | Lactic acid is the cause, cleared in an hour | *Lactic acid does not cause it | Stretching is the cause
